Title: Restore the pre-Chrome-Refresh-2023 menu look
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo), ported from Thorium
Upstream-Source: electron-migrate/thorium-2024-ui-core.patch

Chrome Refresh 2023 made menus large, round and widely spaced. That reads as
native on macOS and as nothing at all on Windows, least of all Windows 7 and 8,
where Electron apps are claiming to draw native menus. This restores the older
metrics.

Ported from Thorium rather than copied. Three differences, all deliberate:

  * Unconditional, where Thorium gates everything on features::IsThorium2024().
    The flag exists so Thorium can ship both looks; this build only wants one,
    and carrying it would mean porting Thorium's ui_base_features hunks as well
    for a switch nobody here would flip.

  * Only the ui/ side. Of the 57 files Thorium's patch touches, 38 are under
    chrome/browser and describe UI that Electron does not compile or display,
    and three more are WebUI CSS for chrome:// pages Electron does not have.
    The toggle_button, combobox, editable_combobox and tree_view changes are
    Chrome-settings widgets that an Electron app never shows either.

  * Restructured for Chromium 152. Thorium's GetCornerRadiusMetric hunk
    switches on ShapeContextTokens directly; upstream now maps context tokens
    to ShapeSysTokens first and switches on those, so the override had to move
    to the top of the function.

What each file does:

  ui/views/layout/layout_provider.cc
                          returns a zero radius for kMenuRadius and
                          kMenuAuxRadius, which upstream maps to kMediumSmall
                          (12px). This is the change that actually squares the
                          menus off: MenuConfig::corner_radius and
                          auxiliary_corner_radius are initialised from these
                          tokens (see menu_config.h), so everything else
                          follows. Not done by editing the token map, which has
                          no "no radius" token -- kDefault means "missing
                          mapping" and trips a DCHECK. kMenuTouchRadius stays
                          rounded, as touch menus should be.

  ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config.cc
                          the cross-platform metrics in InitCommon(): tighter
                          item margins and separators, no item horizontal
                          border padding, and an outer border. Upstream's value
                          is in a comment beside each one so the diff stays
                          readable as a set of deltas.

  ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config_win.cc
                          the Windows metrics, split on version. Windows 11
                          draws rounded menus natively, so it keeps a small
                          radius and the Refresh-era paddings; everything older
                          gets the classic square menu. use_bubble_border keys
                          off corner_radius, so the older path turns the bubble
                          border off by itself.

  ui/views/controls/menu/menu_item_view.cc
                          the classic triangular submenu arrow instead of the
                          Refresh chevron. components/vector_icons already
                          ships submenu_arrow_old.icon and lists it in its
                          BUILD.gn, so no resource work was needed.

Verified by building ui/views:views. The look itself is unverified -- it needs
eyes on a real menu, which is also the only way to judge the metrics.

diff --git a/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config.cc b/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config.cc
index a711c503287a7..0370f0e84fbfe 100644
--- a/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config.cc
+++ b/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config.cc
@@ -85,14 +85,17 @@ void MenuConfig::InitCommon() {
   context_menu_font_list = font_list = TypographyProvider::Get().GetFont(
       style::CONTEXT_MENU, style::STYLE_BODY_3);
   reserve_dedicated_arrow_column = false;
-  menu_horizontal_border_size = 0;
-  submenu_horizontal_overlap = 0;
-  item_vertical_margin = 6;
-  item_horizontal_border_padding = 12;
+  // Pre-Chrome-Refresh-2023 metrics: tighter items and separators, and an
+  // outer border, which is what a native-looking menu wants. Upstream's values
+  // are in the comment beside each.
+  menu_horizontal_border_size = 1;        // 0
+  submenu_horizontal_overlap = -1;        // 0
+  item_vertical_margin = 4;               // 6
+  item_horizontal_border_padding = 0;     // 12
   arrow_size = 16;
-  separator_height = 17;
-  separator_spacing_height = 4;
-  use_outer_border = false;
+  separator_height = 11;                  // 17
+  separator_spacing_height = 3;           // 4
+  use_outer_border = true;                // false
 }
 
 // static
diff --git a/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config_win.cc b/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config_win.cc
index a2dae078ccbd3..c19e99cad988c 100644
--- a/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config_win.cc
+++ b/ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config_win.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #include <Vssym32.h>
 
+#include "base/win/windows_version.h"
 #include "ui/gfx/system_fonts_win.h"
 
 namespace views {
@@ -22,8 +23,42 @@ void MenuConfig::InitPlatform() {
        show_cues == TRUE);
 
   SystemParametersInfo(SPI_GETMENUSHOWDELAY, 0, &show_delay, 0);
-  separator_upper_height = 5;
-  separator_lower_height = 7;
+
+  // Pre-Chrome-Refresh-2023 Windows metrics, ported from Thorium. Windows 11
+  // draws rounded menus natively, so it keeps a small radius and the tighter
+  // Refresh-era paddings; everything older gets the classic square menu, which
+  // is the whole point on Windows 7 and 8.
+  static const bool is_win11 =
+      base::win::GetVersion() >= base::win::Version::WIN11;
+
+  use_outer_border = true;
+  nonrounded_menu_vertical_border_size = 3;
+
+  if (is_win11) {
+    corner_radius = 8;
+    arrow_to_edge_padding = 4;
+    menu_horizontal_border_size = 4;
+    submenu_horizontal_overlap = 1;
+    rounded_menu_vertical_border_size = 4;
+    item_horizontal_padding = 8;
+    between_item_vertical_padding = 2;
+    separator_height = 1;
+    separator_upper_height = 1;
+    separator_lower_height = 1;
+    item_corner_radius = 4;
+  } else {
+    corner_radius = 0;
+    arrow_to_edge_padding = 2;
+    menu_horizontal_border_size = 3;
+    submenu_horizontal_overlap = 0;
+    item_vertical_margin = 3;
+    item_horizontal_border_padding = 0;
+    icon_label_spacing = 10;
+    separator_height = 5;
+    separator_upper_height = 3;
+    separator_lower_height = 3;
+    separator_spacing_height = 2;
+  }
 
   use_bubble_border = corner_radius > 0;
 }
